From b14eca5b53bac3f865e2b05d43ccc47e3015259f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: crazynucfan <127292955+crazynucfan@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 17:50:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 19/20] power: supply: add read-only CellWise CW2217 fuel gauge

Expose the running CW2217 state-of-charge, voltage, signed current,
temperature, cycle count and state-of-health estimate through
power_supply. Check the chip identity, firmware family, active mode,
loaded-profile flag and ready state. Propagate transport and
readiness errors rather than returning invented readings, and retry
words whose high byte rolled over.

Do not reset the chip or load a generic battery profile: the
bootloader already initialized the battery-specific profile on
rhodep. Forbid register writes in regmap and require an explicit
current-sense resistor. A read-only module parameter supplies that
resistor for reversible I2C new_device trials without a firmware
node. Firmware devices use the DT property.

Register units follow the CW2217 support in the vendor reference:
https://github.com/rockchip-linux/kernel/blob/develop-6.1/drivers/power/supply/cw221x_battery.c

The supplied tests compile the actual driver routines with a fake
read-only transport, cover all signed current values, register
rollover, readiness and I2C errors, and verify the sampled rhodep
units.
